From 388603682e97dbf626341cc3589f6d958c57b896 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:31:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 312/314] hir: comparing a const argument whose expression is
 being typechecked doesn't assert

    impl<T> Rd for S<T> where Implicit<T, 0>: Rd, Implicit<T, 1>: Rd { .. }

    mrustc: src/hir/expr_ptr.hpp:55: HIR::ExprNode& HIR::ExprPtrInner::operator*(): Assertion `ptr' failed.

Constant Evaluate typechecks the first bound's `0` (get_or_gen_mir), and
Typecheck_Code holds the expression's root node meanwhile. That typecheck
indexes the impl's bounds, which compares the two bounds' Unevaluated
const arguments, and ConstGeneric_Unevaluated::ord dereferenced both root
nodes (to see whether both are a const param). An absent root is now just
not a const param; the comparison goes on with the printed form, which
already shows it as `/*NULL*/`.

Found with C170 (next commit): cryptography-x509 0.1.0's derived impls have
bounds for `#[implicit(0)]` and `#[implicit(1)]` variants; before it, the
crate failed earlier in Resolve UFCS. Any item with two where-bounds with
literal const arguments hit this.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

diff --git a/src/hir/hir.cpp b/src/hir/hir.cpp
index 14086e57..6c577faa 100644
--- a/src/hir/hir.cpp
+++ b/src/hir/hir.cpp
@@ -123,8 +123,11 @@ namespace HIR {
 
             // HACK: If the inner is a const param on both, sort based on that.
             // - Very similar to the ordering of TypeRef::Generic
-            const auto* tn = dynamic_cast<const HIR::ExprNode_ConstParam*>(&**this->expr);
-            const auto* xn = dynamic_cast<const HIR::ExprNode_ConstParam*>(&**x.expr);
+            // - An expression being typechecked has no root node (Typecheck_Code holds it), and the impl's bounds are
+            //   indexed - so compared - during that typecheck: `where Implicit<T, 0>: R, Implicit<T, 1>: R` asserted
+            //   while evaluating the `0` (cryptography-x509 0.1.0 extensions.rs, asn1_derive 0.24.1)
+            const auto* tn = *this->expr ? dynamic_cast<const HIR::ExprNode_ConstParam*>(&**this->expr) : nullptr;
+            const auto* xn = *x.expr ? dynamic_cast<const HIR::ExprNode_ConstParam*>(&**x.expr) : nullptr;
             if( tn && xn )
             {
                 // Is this valid? What if they're from different scopes?
